Roku is changing how the world watches TV

Roku is the #1 TV streaming platform in the U.S., Canada, and Mexico, and we've set our sights on powering every television in the world. Roku pioneered streaming to the TV. Our mission is to be the TV streaming platform that connects the entire TV ecosystem. We connect consumers to the content they love, enable content publishers to build and monetize large audiences, and provide advertisers unique capabilities to engage consumers.

From your first day at Roku, you'll make a valuable - and valued - contribution. We're a fast-growing public company where no one is a bystander. We offer you the opportunity to delight millions of TV streamers around the world while gaining meaningful experience across a variety of disciplines.

&nbsp;

What does the team work on?&nbsp;

At Roku, we&nbsp;like&nbsp;to say that there are no bystanders, and that is as true in the advertising team as it is in any other&nbsp;facet&nbsp;of the company. We work together to ensure our clients understand this new world of advertising, that they are making the best possible decisions to support their own goals, and drive advertiser interest and engagement across the board. The Client Services team&nbsp;is responsible for&nbsp;managing and growing Roku's partnerships with Advertisers and&nbsp;ultimately enabling&nbsp;our clients to reach their business&nbsp;objectives.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What is the role?&nbsp;

The Senior Manager, Client Services is a leadership role responsible for overseeing the strategic account management function within Roku's advertising organization. This role is central to maintaining and expanding client relationships, ensuring the delivery of effective advertising solutions, and driving the overall growth of client partnerships. The Senior Manager will lead a team focused on executing high-volume, high-impact direct and programmatic campaigns, with an emphasis on cultivating strong relationships with performance-minded Media and Entertainment partners. This individual will be responsible for driving incremental revenue, upselling opportunities, and revenue retention across their team's portfolio. The role requires close collaboration with cross-functional teams to ensure operational excellence, efficient resource allocation, and alignment with client objectives. The Senior Manager will also implement performance metrics and reporting systems to monitor and continuously improve team and client outcomes.&nbsp;

For New York Only - The estimated annual total cash for this position is between $171,500 - $209,700. This cash range includes on-target earnings from commission.&nbsp;Compensation packages are based on factors unique to each candidate, including but not limited to skill set, certifications, and specific geographical location.&nbsp;This role is eligible for health insurance, equity awards, life insurance, disability benefits, parental leave, wellness benefits, and paid time off.

&nbsp;

How will I use AI&nbsp;at&nbsp;Roku?&nbsp;

At Roku, we&nbsp;don't&nbsp;just use AI, we work with it. AI agents and smart tools help power drafts, analysis, and repetitive workflows, while our people bring direction, judgment, and accountability.&nbsp;

